From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:12:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Aim at enemies above and below like DOOM

Nothing looks up and down on the DS, the shots were only aimed at an
enemy within a cone of 21.6 degrees around the view, up and down as
much as to the side, so enemies on stairs, ledges and in pits were
missed. Like in DOOM only the angle to the side counts now, still at
most 21.6 degrees, an enemy in sight above or below is hit.
---
 WinQuake/pr_cmds.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/WinQuake/pr_cmds.c b/WinQuake/pr_cmds.c
index 3593bb9..40270ec 100644
--- a/WinQuake/pr_cmds.c
+++ b/WinQuake/pr_cmds.c
@@ -1327,13 +1327,16 @@ PF_aim
 
 Pick a vector for the player to shoot along
 vector aim(entity, missilespeed)
+
+There is no looking up and down, so like in DOOM only the angle to the
+side counts: sv_aim is its cosine, an enemy in sight above or below is hit
 =============
 */
 cvar_t	sv_aim = {"sv_aim", "0.93"};
 void PF_aim (void)
 {
 	edict_t	*ent, *check, *bestent;
-	vec3_t	start, dir, end, bestdir;
+	vec3_t	start, dir, end, bestdir, flat;
 	int		i, j;
 	trace_t	tr;
 	float	dist, bestdist;
@@ -1359,6 +1362,9 @@ void PF_aim (void)
 
 // try all possible entities
 	VectorCopy (dir, bestdir);
+	VectorCopy (dir, flat);
+	flat[2] = 0;
+	VectorNormalize (flat);
 	bestdist = sv_aim.value;
 	bestent = NULL;
 	
@@ -1375,8 +1381,9 @@ void PF_aim (void)
 			end[j] = check->v.origin[j]
 			+ 0.5*(check->v.mins[j] + check->v.maxs[j]);
 		VectorSubtract (end, start, dir);
+		dir[2] = 0;
 		VectorNormalize (dir);
-		dist = DotProduct (dir, pr_global_struct->v_forward);
+		dist = DotProduct (dir, flat);
 		if (dist < bestdist)
 			continue;	// to far to turn
 		tr = SV_Move (start, vec3_origin, vec3_origin, end, false, ent);
